**CLAUSE 19 — OBLIGATIONS OF THE GRANTEE**

(a) The Grantee shall implement the Project in accordance with the Project Description set out in Schedule A and the Budget set out in Schedule B, subject to such variations as may be approved in writing by Harbor City Fund from time to time.

(b) The Grantee shall:

(i) use the Grant Funds solely for the purposes of the Project and in accordance with the Budget;

(ii) maintain accurate and complete books and records of all income and expenditure relating to the Project, and retain such books and records for a period of at least five (5) years after the end of the Project;

(iii) submit the Reports in accordance with the Reporting Schedule set out in Schedule C;

(iv) obtain and maintain all necessary licences, permits, and approvals required for the conduct of the Project in Singapore;

(v) comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and guidelines, including but not limited to the Charities Act 1994, the Code of Governance for Charities and IPCs, and the Personal Data Protection Act 2012;

(vi) ensure that all publicity, promotional materials, and publications relating to the Project acknowledge the support of Harbor City Fund in a form acceptable to Harbor City Fund; and

(vii) notify Harbor City Fund in writing within ten (10) business days of any matter that materially affects the Grantee’s ability to perform its obligations under this Agreement, including any actual or anticipated delay, cost overrun, or change in Project scope.

**CLAUSE 20 — BENEFICIARY TARGETS AND REPORTING**

(a) The Grantee shall use its best efforts to achieve the beneficiary targets set out in Schedule A (the “Beneficiary Targets”).

(b) BrightPath Community Kitchens aims for a beneficiary_target of 5000 people. Record status: current. This target represents the cumulative number of unique individuals who will receive services under the Project over the Project Period. For the avoidance of doubt, an individual who receives services more than once shall be counted only once for the purpose of the Beneficiary Targets.

(c) The Beneficiary Targets are a commitment under this Agreement. The Grantee shall report on its progress towards the Beneficiary Targets in each Report, and shall provide such supporting data as Harbor City Fund may reasonably request, including but not limited to attendance records, registration lists, and survey data. All data shall be anonymised or aggregated where necessary to comply with the Personal Data Protection Act 2012.

(d) The Grantee shall target the following communities in Singapore:

(i) low-income families residing in public rental housing in the following areas: Bedok, Geylang, Jurong West, and Woodlands;

(ii) elderly persons aged 60 and above who are living alone or with limited family support, particularly those referred by social service agencies;

(iii) persons with disabilities and their caregivers, including those receiving services from voluntary welfare organisations; and

(iv) migrant workers residing in dormitories or other temporary accommodation, with a focus on those engaged in the construction, marine, and process sectors.

(e) The Grantee shall reach the communities described in Clause 20(d) through the following methods:

(i) partnerships with community centres, residents’ committees, and grassroots organisations in the identified areas;

(ii) referrals from social service agencies, hospitals, and family service centres;

(iii) direct outreach at locations frequented by the target communities, including markets, coffeeshops, and community clubs;

(iv) collaboration with dormitory operators and migrant worker welfare organisations; and

(v) publicity through community notice boards, social media, and radio broadcasts in relevant languages, including Mandarin, Malay, Tamil, and Bengali.

(f) The Grantee shall maintain a beneficiary tracking system that records, for each beneficiary: the date of first service, the type of service provided, and the beneficiary’s demographic category. The Grantee shall not disclose any personal data of beneficiaries except as required for the purposes of this Agreement or as required by law.
